## Branches and PRs

- Branch name: `claude/<linear-id-lowercase>-<short-slug>`, e.g. `claude/abc-12-search-page`. The Linear ID in the name lets Linear link the branch.
- One issue, one PR. Keep PRs small. Open as a draft, mark ready when checks pass.
- The PR body starts with `Fixes ABC-12` (the Linear ID) so Linear links and closes the issue.
- Never push to `main`. Never merge your own PR unless the PR has the `auto-merge` label, all checks are green (including `Merge gate`), it has no `needs-human` label, every review thread is resolved, and the latest Claude review ends "Verdict: ready to merge". Just before merging, re-run the gate (`gh workflow run merge-gate.yml --ref <branch> -f pr=<number>`) and wait for it to pass, because it can be stale. Never resolve a security thread you did not fix; leave it for a person.

## Build and test

- All checks: `./scripts/check.sh` (CI runs the same script).
